/**
 * @mainpage BrickGame Documentation
 *
 * ## Overview
 * This repository contains two small classic games implemented in C/C++:
 * - Tetris (C + NCurses)
 * - Snake (C++ - modular design: model/controller/frontend)
 *
 * The documentation generated here includes both projects and their
 * unit tests and should help developers understand the project layout
 * and public interfaces.
 *
 * ## Table of Contents
 * - [Tetris](#tetris)
 * - [Snake](#snake)
 * - [Installation](#installation)
 * - [Usage](#usage)
 * - [Testing](#testing)
 */

/**
 * @section tetris Tetris
 * The Tetris game is implemented in C and lives under `brick_game/tetris/`.
 * It uses NCurses for console rendering and includes unit tests under `tests/tetris_tests/`.
 */

/**
 * @section snake Snake
 * The Snake game is implemented in modern C++ and lives under `brick_game/snake/`.
 * Key components:
 * - `model/` — game logic, snake model, and state machine
 * - `controller/` — input and high-level orchestration
 * - `gui/cli/renderer.c` — shared CLI renderer used by both games
 *
 * Controls (CLI): arrow keys to move, P to pause, Q to quit.
 */

/**
 * @section installation Installation
 * 
 * ### Prerequisites
 * - GCC / G++
 * - NCurses
 * - Make
 * - CMake (for desktop builds)
 * - GoogleTest / Check (for unit tests)
 *
 * ### Steps
 * 1. From `src/` run:
 *    ```
 *    make install
 *    ```
 * 2. To build only Snake (console):
 *    ```
 *    make snake
 *    ```
 */

/**
 * @section usage Usage
 * Run the console builds from `src/`:
 * - Tetris console: `./build/tetris_console`
 * - Snake console:  `./build/snake_console`
 */

/**
 * @section testing Testing
 * Unit tests are located in `tests/` for both games. From `src/` run:
 * ```
 * make test
 * ```
 * This will run test binaries under `build/` produced by the Makefile.
 */
